Ok, I now know more after getting some things to work and can ask a better question.

I've been able to get the contents of a data frame using the REXP and RList classes to display the column names and data points. Now, I'd like to modify the data frame. It's not clear how to do this. It looks like I need to use RVector which extends the old fashion java Vector class. For example how would I change a variable name or data element ? 

REXP r = c.eval("read.table(...)");
RList rList = r.asList();

String var = rList.at(j);
String data = rList.at(j).asStrings()[i];

//for example, modify r using Java and then do
c.assign("df", r);  
REXP r = c.eval("plot(df)");
out.write(r.asBytes());

I assume it's proper to modify an REXP and then still be able to send it back to R and use it to create a plot, save it for later, etc. Or do I have to use R to modify a data frame e.g. c.eval('colnames(df) <- c("x", "y", "z")'); ?

For performance reasons I'd like to minimize trips back to R to do things. My app is highly interactive and it may not always be able to do everything all at once.

